export const title = "FTP Upload";
export const html = "<h1>FTP Upload</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>An action type that lets you upload event snapshots to an FTP server when an application event occurs. The directory and file name used to store the snapshot file can be set variably using the event's metadata.</p>\n\n<p>An FTP Upload action can be added from the action settings screen.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>FTP</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to <strong>FTP</strong> reveals the related settings below it.</p>\n\n<h2>Snapshot Time Range Settings</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:150px 1fr 40px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;align-items:center;\">\n    <span>Snapshot Time Range</span><input value=\"-2\" disabled style=\"width:60px;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;\">~</span><span><input value=\"1\" disabled style=\"width:60px;\"> second(s)</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Sets the time range of upload snapshots based on the event time. With the example setting above, snapshots generated from 2 seconds before the event to 1 second after the event are uploaded.</p>\n<p>Separately from event-time snapshots, periodic snapshots are generated for each channel at a minimum rate of 1 per second.</p>\n\n<h2>Snapshot Upload Directory and File Name Format Settings</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr 60px;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Directory</span><input value=\"{{TIME YYYYMMDD}}/{{TIME %HH}}\" disabled><span></span>\n    <span>Filename</span><input value=\"{{TIME YYYYMMDD}}_{{TIME HHMMSS}}\" disabled><span>.jpg</span>\n    <span>Example</span><span style=\"grid-column:span 2;font-family:monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted);\">20220902/15/20220902_153702.jpg</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Directory and filename settings, with token examples</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>The directory setting specifies where the snapshot image is stored when the FTP Upload action runs.</p>\n<p>The setting can include event metadata. If you include time data in the path setting as in the example above, the upload directory is set based on the time the event occurred. If not set, the snapshot is saved to the FTP connection's root directory.</p>\n\n<p>The snapshot file name can be set the same way as the directory.</p>\n<p>The extension is automatically set to <code>.jpg</code> when specifying the snapshot file name, so you don't need to enter it separately.</p>\n\n<p>Once you've set the snapshot file name, the Example field shows a preview of the snapshot path generated by the configured directory and file name.</p>\n\n<h2>FTP Server Settings</h2>\n<p>Add the FTP server settings you want to upload to under the Server item.</p>\n<p>Once added, an FTP server setting can be used when configuring other rules or when setting up FTP Upload actions in other apps.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:120px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add</span></div>\n<p>Click the Add button to add a new server setting.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:420px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">FTP Server</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Protocol</span><span><label><input type=\"radio\" checked disabled> FTP</label> <label><input type=\"radio\" disabled> SFTP</label></span>\n      <span>Name</span><input value=\"My FTP Server\" disabled>\n      <span>Host</span><input value=\"192.168.0.5\" disabled>\n      <span>Port</span><input value=\"21\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input value=\"myftpuser\" disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input value=\"mypassword\" disabled>\n      <span>Passive Mode</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>FTP server configuration</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>Enter the target FTP server's information and click the <strong>Apply</strong> button to apply the settings.</p>\n<p>Once an FTP server setting is added, a new item appears in the FTP server list.</p>\n<p>Check the target server item in the list to complete the server setting.</p>";
